vllm.cpp: VT_DFLASH_HOST=1 — the DFlash draft forward runs on the HOST (CPU thread pool) over host-resident weights; the draft trunk is NOT staged to the device. The residual taps download once per propose (outside the captured verify region) and the k draft tokens upload back. The device keeps the verify, the GDN state and the KV pool.
vllm.cpp: VT_DFLASH_DRAFT=1 — the DFlash2 draft proposes through the DIRECT-ARGMAX arm (bundle dflash2.py has_selector=false): full-vocab argmax per block row, candidate selector NOT resident (~254 MB freed). The verify stays lossless (greedy accept = the target's argmax); only acceptance can differ from the selector arm.
